# Activity scene — visiting the grandparent, second time. cast.md § 3.3: "A
# photo album scene where the grandparent talks about people who have died";
# "Drops lines that suggest they see more than they say — usually one
# sentence per visit." She does not speak ill of the organization.
# TODO: authenticity check

The photo album comes out. {GameState.grandparent_word} turns the pages slowly, naming everyone.
"That's your grandfather at the convention in the old stadium. Look at that tie." "That's the Hendersons. Both gone now. Resting, until the resurrection."
She stops on a picture of a young woman laughing at something off to the side of the frame. She doesn't name her. She turns the page.
- "Who was that?"
	[signal arg="EXPOSE:1"]
	"Oh — that's Ruth. We were in the same service group for years." She smooths the plastic over the next page. "Ruth left. A long time ago." A pause. "I still think about her. Isn't that silly?"
- Let her turn the page.
	You let her turn the page. The next one is your {GameState.parent_word} as a baby, asleep in a laundry basket under the seats at an assembly, and she laughs at herself for having kept it.
